                <pb facs="0928" n="792" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg792"/>

                <head>No. 561.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L. S. Sackville West to Mr.
                        Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-03-19"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 19.</date>
                        (Received March 20.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that the
                    Marquis of Salisbury has requested me, by telegraph, to represent to you the
                    very great importance which Her Majesty’s Government attach to the presence of a
                    delegate from the United States Government at the approaching sugar conference
                    which opens on the 5th April next, and that the negotiations can not be carried
                    to a successful issue unless the United States take part in them.</p>
                <p>Trusting that you will give this matter your early attention,</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">L. S. Sackville
                    West.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
